5. Denial or Cancellation of Entry visa
\par 
\par An entry visa may be denied or canceled if the applicant or the holder: 
\par 1. has no visible means of support or is likely to become a public burden; 
\par 2. is found to be a notorious criminal. 
\par 3. has been declared to be a drug addict;' 
\par 4. has been suspected of suffering from a dangerous contagious disease; 
\par 5. has been found to be a threat to the security of Ethiopia; 
\par 6. has furnished fraudulent information; or 
\par 7. has violated the provisions of this Proclamation or Regulations issued here under.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid7099086 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\lang1033\langfe1033\langnp1033\langfenp1033\insrsid7099086 
