\par 
\par A foreigner who applies to acquire Ethiopian nationality
\par By law shall:
\par 1/ have attained the age of majority and be legally
\par capable under the Ethiopian law;
\par 2/ have established his domicile in Ethiopia and have
\par lived in Ethiopia for a total of at least four years
\par preceding the submission of his application;
\par 3/ be able to communicate in anyone of the languages
\par of the nations/nationalities of the Country;
\par 4/ have sufficient and lawful source of income to
\par maintain himself and his family;
\par 5/ be a person of good character;
\par 6/ have no record of criminal conviction;
\par 7/ be able to show that he has been released from his
\par previous nationality or the possibility of obtaining
\par such a release upon the acquisition of Ethiopian
\par nationality or that he is a stateless person; and
\par 8/ be required to take the oath of allegiance stated under
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang1035\langfe1033\langnp1035\langfenp1033\insrsid15600833\charrsid15600833 Article 12 of this Proclamation.
